Komodo Health Privacy Notice

Komodo Health, Inc., and its affiliates (collectively, “we,” “our,” “us,” or “Komodo Health”) are committed to protecting your privacy and Personal Data about you. This Privacy Notice is intended to describe our practices regarding collection, use, and sharing of Personal Data relating to visitors to the Komodo Health website (www.komodohealth.com, the “Site”), product users, customers, prospective and former customers, business partners, and healthcare professionals. Where we refer to “Personal Data” throughout this Privacy Notice, we mean “Personal Data” or “Personal Information” as such terms are defined in applicable an applicable law or regulation. 

Personal Data Collected

When You Communicate With Us

When you communicate with us in and through the Site, email us, or otherwise communicate with us, we collect the following identifiers or professional information that may, alone or in combination with other information, constitute Personal Data:

Name, company name, job title, state/region;
Contact information such as email address and phone number; and
Content of communications sent to us.

When You Request Information From Us
When you use features such as “Contact” or “Request Demo” on the Site, we collect the following identifiers or professional information that may, alone or in combination with other information, constitute Personal Data:

Name, company name, job title, state/region;
Contact information such as email address and phone number; and
Which of our data products and services (collectively, our “Services”) may interest you.

When We Collect Healthcare Provider Personal Data
In connection with our Services, we collect the following professional information or identifiers about healthcare providers from third party sources and publicly available sources. Some of this information may, alone or in combination with other information, constitute Personal Data:

Name, company name, affiliated institution names, job title, professional credentials;
National Provider Identifier (NPI); and
Contact information such as email address, office address, fax number, and phone number.

Healthcare Provider Correction and Appeal Requests
If you use the Provider Correction and Appeal Request form available through https://www.komodohealth.com/provider-correction-and-appeal-request you must provide:

Name;
Organization;
NPI;
Contact information such as email address and phone number; and
Correction request details.

Professional or Employment-Related Information
If you approach us with respect to our career opportunities, we collect the following professional or employment-related information that may, alone or in combination with other information, constitute Personal Information:

Name;
Contact information such as email address and phone number;
Personal Information included in the resume/CV and cover letter; and
Personal Information included in your public LinkedIn profile.

Customer and User Data
If you are a representative of a current, former, or prospective customer or a user of our Services or the Site, we collect the following information that may, alone or in combination with other information, constitute Personal Data:

Name, contact information (e.g., business email address and phone number, etc.), job title and/or job function, and company name;
Account usage, login credentials, and device information collected during or from your usage of our Services (e.g., username, IP address, device type, browser version, locale, language settings, user activity logs, session IDs, connectivity, technical, and aggregated usage data, etc.); and
Our communications and correspondences with you, including sensory information such as audio and video recordings and transcriptions of meetings and transcriptions and analyses and inferences derived from such correspondences and sensory information; 

Internet Activity Information
Software used on the Site collects Internet or other electronic network activity information that may, alone or in combination with other information, constitute Personal Data:

The domain from which you access the Site;
The type of browser and operating system used in the device you use to access the Site;
Internet Protocol (IP) address;
The date and time you visited the Site (time stamp);
The website used to link to the Site from;
Any search terms used to navigate the Site;
The language used in browsing the Site in social media applications;
A browsing session ID; and
Whether you are a first time visitor to the Site.
Sources of Personal Data

In the last 12 months, we have collected Personal Data from the following categories of sources:

You: information collected directly from you;
Software: information automatically collected via cookies, web logs, web beacons, and other software-based analytics tools;
Publicly available sources;
Commercial partners: information obtained from our data licensors and commercial partners, including commercial data aggregators; and:
Commercial resources: other commercially available resources, such as medical publications.
How the Personal Data is Used

We use Personal Data about you for the following purposes:

To operate and improve our Site, including through analytics to help us understand how you use the Site, so that we can present content in the best manner;
To provide the Services to you;
To operate, develop, support, and improve our Services;
To provide you with any information that you request from us. If you do not provide us with the information we need to respond to your request, we may not be able to provide you with the information that you request from us;
To carry out internal business operations. For example, financial reporting, internal reporting and business modeling purposes (e.g., forecasting, product strategy), analysis of conversion rates, sales, system usage, marketing effectiveness, training, customer and account management, as well as for other business analytics projects and internal reporting. 
To notify you about changes to the Site and our Services;
To enable us to issue a notice, administrative, or corrective action to you in relation to the Site or the Services, if required;
To send you direct marketing messages that you have consented to receive;
To protect against, identify, and prevent fraud and other unlawful activity, claims, and other liabilities;
To comply with applicable legal and regulatory requirements, industry standards, and our own policies; and
Where permitted by law, to provide you with information about other products and services we offer that are similar to those that you have already subscribed to or inquired about and we feel may interest you.
